[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
Hadoop ships its configuration as sample files.  Before starting any daemon,
copy the ones you need into %%ETCDIR%% and edit them:

  cd %%ETCDIR%%
  for f in *.sample; do cp -n "$f" "${f%.sample}"; done
  cp %%EXAMPLESDIR%%/conf/hdfs-site.xml %%EXAMPLESDIR%%/conf/mapred-site.xml \
     %%EXAMPLESDIR%%/conf/yarn-site.xml %%ETCDIR%%/

%%EXAMPLESDIR%% also holds the full *-default.xml files for reference.

Format the HDFS metadata once, as the %%HDFS_USER%% user, before the first
namenode start:

  su -m %%HDFS_USER%% -c 'sh -c "%%PREFIX%%/bin/hdfs --config %%ETCDIR%% namenode -format"'

The daemons run as %%HDFS_USER%% (HDFS) and %%MAPRED_USER%% (YARN/MapReduce)
and log to %%HADOOP_LOGDIR%%.  Enable the ones you need, for example:

  sysrc namenode_enable=YES datanode_enable=YES
  service namenode start
  service datanode start

Available services: namenode datanode secondarynamenode journalnode zkfc
resourcemanager nodemanager webappproxyserver historyserver
EOM
}
]
